# DESK42 -- the STRENAME retry loop of the rebuilt ADFFINFO box.
# STRENAME alert, so this run's own [alert] dump gives its button click points.
#
# The failure is EmuTOS's own ordering: OK writes the attribute first
# (`dos_chmod`, deskinf.c:591-605) and renames afterwards (`:616-626`), and a
# Read-Only file cannot be renamed (`xrename`: `if (fcb->f_attrib & FA_RO)
# return EACCDN`, bdos/fsdir.c:943-944).  So one dialog pass that ticks
# Read-Only *and* shortens the name ends in `STRENAME`.
100 parkbr
300 move 600 240
1000 arm
1200 mark A_IDLE
1600 move 38 35
1800 down
1803 up
1810 down
1813 up
2400 move 600 240
3200 mark B_WIN1
3600 move 179 271
4000 down
4003 up
4400 parkbr
5000 mark B2_FILESEL
5400 move 88 240
5600 move 88 9
6200 move 152 43
6800 down
7000 up
7600 parkbr
8600 mark C_FILEINFO
9000 move 396 305
9400 down
9600 up
10000 parkbr
10800 mark D_RONLY
11200 key 0E
11220 key 8E
11800 mark E_SHORTNAME
12200 move 216 353
12600 down
12800 up
13400 parkbr
14400 mark F_STRENAME
# -- Retry (272,269 from this measurement's d42d1 [alert] dump): the `while(1)`
#    of deskinf.c:551-635 re-shows the *same* box with the attempted name still
#    in the field and the now-written Read-Only attribute selected.  Cancel
#    then leaves it (424,353 from the d42b [dlg] dump).
14800 move 272 269
15200 down
15400 up
16000 parkbr
17000 mark G_RETRY
17400 move 424 353
17800 down
18000 up
18600 parkbr
19600 mark H_END
